      "framing": "sensitivity",
      "window_provenance": "sourced",
      "basis": "Model meaning: fraction of charged power deposited in the blanket circuits, remainder to the divertor. Inherited 0.25 is assumption A1. Lyon Table IV prints 98.1 MW to the divertor of 487 MW charged power; Raffray Table V implies 66.8 MW of nuclear heating in the divertor at 2365 MW (186 minus 24 friction, 23.6 conducted, 23.6 alpha loss, 48 radiated), 68.8 MW scaled to 2436 MW. Divertor deposition 167 MW gives 1 minus 167/487.2 = 0.657; the nuclear share is carried as charged power because the model has no divertor nuclear-heating term.",
      "missing_response": "No radiation, scrape-off-layer or neutron transport model resists the partition.",
